@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create orders and administrators can create coupons, but nothing connects the
+two: an order always keeps its full amount and the `coupons` / `coupon_redemptions` tables are
+never used at redemption time. Orders need a way to apply a coupon so the discount is
+calculated, validated and persisted in one place.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": "SAVE20" }`.
+- Validate the coupon before discounting: it must exist, be `ACTIVE`, and the order amount must
+  be greater than or equal to the coupon's `minAmountCents`.
+- Reject coupons used outside their validity window, including expired coupons
+  (`validUntil` already passed relative to the injected `Clock`).
+- Calculate the discount by coupon type: `FIXED` subtracts a fixed amount, `PERCENT` takes a
+  percentage of the order amount (capped by `maxDiscountCents` when set).
+- Persist the result on the order (`discount_cents`, `final_amount_cents`, `coupon_code`) and
+  record the redemption in `coupon_redemptions`, incrementing `coupons.used_count`.
+- Return the updated order on success (HTTP 200); return HTTP 400 for an unusable coupon.
+- Orders that already carry a coupon may be re-priced: applying another coupon replaces the
+  previous discount, always calculated from the original order amount.
+
+Out of scope: usage-limit enforcement (`usage_limit` / `used_count` are still incremented for
+auditing), order status transitions, and coupon removal/reversal.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `coupon-redemption`: applying a coupon to an order at HTTP level - endpoint contract,
+  coupon eligibility rules, discount calculation, and persistence of the redemption.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None. The existing coupon administration and order lifecycle behavior is unchanged.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/routes/orders.ts`: register the new `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` route.
+- `src/services/orderService.ts`: apply the coupon to an order, orchestrating order + coupon
+  services.
+- `src/services/couponService.ts`: coupon eligibility rules and discount calculation.
+- `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts`: persist discount, final amount and coupon code.
+- `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts`: append a redemption row and increment `used_count`.
+- `src/app.ts`: inject the coupon side of the domain into order handling.
+- No schema change: `orders`, `coupons` and `coupon_redemptions` already support everything
+  required.
+- No change to `TASK.md` or the existing tests.
